    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0756" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">365.1121 Slavich, Nickola/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-10T12:00:00+01:00">September 10,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 10—8:35 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>172. The Minister of Foreign Affairs and the Chief of the American Section are on
                    leave. Consequently, while I have transmitted the essence of your No. 133, 4th
                    of September, 5 p.m., the replies will not be immediately forthcoming.</p>
                <p>At the Foreign Office I learned that the procedure relative to the detention and
                    imprisonment of foreigners in Italy has been reviewed <pb facs="0757" n="637"
                        xml:id="pg637"/> by officials of the several Ministries concerned. The final
                    report, however, has not been sent yet to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
